WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language:  en

00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:22.661
It's a morning when I woke up at 5:30, still dimly lit.

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:31.865
I got up, washed my face, brushed my teeth and took care of my skin.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.595
I notice the dryness of the room these days when I feel discomfort in my throat and ears.

00:01:05.568 --> 00:01:12.135
I am wondering if I should buy a humidifier.

00:01:39.227 --> 00:01:45.886
When the new year starts,
I was thinking of learning something physical... 😓

00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:56.298
I'm happy with just watching YouTube and doing some simple stretches to feel like I'm getting something off my back!

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:10.862
I've heard that if you change the time you write in your journal from night to morning, the content will also change.

00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:23.178
I have a list of words I've come across, things to do, mumbo-jumbo in my mind, and
There's no set format, I just write whatever comes to my mind.

00:02:26.358 --> 00:02:32.588
Today I made an ideal time schedule for morning activities.

00:02:50.161 --> 00:02:57.955
The other day I put on a pair of denims that I quickly took from the washing machine and went outside.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:07.957
The hem was so wrinkled.
I spent the rest of the day wishing no one would look at my feet.

00:03:20.053 --> 00:03:27.325
This skirt also comes with a bitter memory that I noticed a furball after I came home after wearing it.

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:40.540
I have a replacement blade for my hairball remover, but I have not been able to change the blade because the cap is no longer removable.

00:03:52.953 --> 00:03:58.662
I'll try to get as far as I can today.

00:04:14.715 --> 00:04:26.187
I've been thinking a lot about hairballs, ironing these days...

00:04:30.644 --> 00:04:42.055
I've already had a satisfying day today, being able to do home cleaners.

00:05:15.704 --> 00:05:24.080
It went by faster than I thought it would.
The sun is shining and it's getting brighter.

00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:11.753
It's more eye-opening to be out in the sun.

00:06:37.198 --> 00:06:49.804
When it's light outside, I finally get dressed and
It's like the day is starting in earnest.

00:06:57.055 --> 00:07:05.492
I make a smoothie with frozen kiwi for breakfast.

00:07:08.926 --> 00:07:19.233
I add a pinch of salt to 100cc of amazake and heat it up.

00:07:23.992 --> 00:07:30.713
Add two kiwis and stir.

00:07:35.848 --> 00:07:43.488
Slightly warm smoothie is ready.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:40.901
This cupboard doesn't fit in the kitchen, so I'm using it here.

00:08:42.661 --> 00:08:48.983
It's still a little inconvenient if it's not right next to the kitchen. 😂

00:09:26.362 --> 00:09:36.332
I bought a great bouquet of recycled flowers from some event!

00:09:38.938 --> 00:09:50.870
I had a bunch of them on display.
I still felt they were too jammed together, so I decided to separate them.😹

00:11:40.936 --> 00:11:46.706
I love the weak scent of the candles when I pass by them.

00:11:51.067 --> 00:11:58.033
I also like the delicate glass that seems to break.🥰

00:12:01.527 --> 00:12:10.117
It's a spoon whose handle doesn't stick to the condiment.🐤

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:25.461
For some reason, my honey jar has been sticky lately, even after wiping it down.

00:12:31.933 --> 00:12:42.578
I found just the cutest jar.

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:05.493
I was so distressed that I put the expiration date on the bottom of the jar.

00:13:14.889 --> 00:13:24.889
I put off washing the canisters and started the new year.

00:13:39.441 --> 00:13:50.146
I put a teaspoon in the salt and a tablespoon in the sugar.

00:14:13.347 --> 00:14:21.048
I accidentally put a cutting board on a still warm induction heating.
I warped the wooden cutting board.

00:14:21.846 --> 00:14:30.344
I bought a new cutting board.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:50.904
I'm still getting used to the new place, and there are a lot of things I want to review here and there, such as storage and what I'm using.

00:14:55.101 --> 00:15:04.550
It's been about a month in the blink of an eye, lol.

00:15:23.853 --> 00:15:29.409
My sister gave me an avocado cutter as a gift.

00:15:34.508 --> 00:15:43.558
I think the avocado was too soft.

00:16:31.054 --> 00:16:40.779
When I cooked junk sandwich,
I wanted to set it with fries anyway.

00:17:00.163 --> 00:17:11.818
Put the potatoes in a bag.
1 tablespoon each of flour and potato starch.

00:17:13.599 --> 00:17:21.668
Add salt and white pepper and shake.

00:17:29.381 --> 00:17:40.730
Put them in the oil before heating and fry them over medium heat.

00:17:45.498 --> 00:17:53.720
Crispy and flaky fries inside.
If you eat a handful, you'll lose a lot in no time. 🤤

00:18:45.761 --> 00:18:57.907
like I feel like I'm on a trip abroad,
Or a brunch complete with an amount of food that will make me feel like I'm about to start a party...

00:19:01.947 --> 00:19:09.648
I was watching the drama while I was eating, and I was horrified at myself for almost eating it all.

00:19:11.815 --> 00:19:21.141
I saved the rest for breakfast tomorrow.

00:19:33.135 --> 00:19:41.358
I knew it was too early for a cold latte, so I heated it up in the microwave.☕😅

00:19:48.463 --> 00:19:55.030
I've always longed to use a glass pen.

00:19:55.704 --> 00:20:01.995
I suddenly saw an ad on Instagram for a glass pen kit and
I found myself buying one.

00:20:28.321 --> 00:20:37.463
It also comes with a watercolor pen set that allows me to draw botanical art.

00:20:44.251 --> 00:20:56.612
It's very helpful for me, as I don't have the artistic ability, to have drafts to practice with.😂

00:22:16.562 --> 00:22:29.290
I lost track of time and just kept moving on to the next step.

00:22:32.865 --> 00:22:43.203
In no time at all, the sun was setting and the room was getting cold.

00:22:51.667 --> 00:23:04.089
That's all for now, and I'll see you next time.

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:24.097
I'm going to make dashi stock with a dashi packet and prepare dinner for the evening.

00:23:58.353 --> 00:24:11.165
Cut 40g each of burdock root and carrot into 1cm cubes.

00:24:15.244 --> 00:24:19.175
80 g chicken meat.

00:24:39.395 --> 00:24:47.066
Put dried shiitake mushrooms back in water overnight.
(In the video I only put them back in for 30 minutes.😂)

00:24:58.551 --> 00:25:09.348
Heat 1 teaspoon of oil and fry the chicken first.

00:25:21.281 --> 00:25:29.657
Add 1 cup of soup stock

00:25:33.909 --> 00:25:37.901
Add shiitake mushroom stock

00:25:39.754 --> 00:25:52.390
1/2 teaspoon salt, 1 teaspoon sugar, 1 tablespoon light soy sauce

00:26:00.977 --> 00:26:09.966
Cut fried tofu in half, swabbed and flipped over.

00:26:18.993 --> 00:26:26.357
Two rice cakes left over from New Year's.

00:26:32.780 --> 00:26:40.512
200㏄ 
Add water if it is not enough

00:27:05.550 --> 00:27:14.140
Bring to a boil over medium heat and when bubbles start to appear.
Stir from the bottom.

00:27:16.774 --> 00:27:22.851
Cover and cook over low heat for 10 minutes

00:27:27.011 --> 00:27:40.261
100g ground pork, 1 tablespoon sake, 1 1/2 tablespoons soy sauce, 1/2 tablespoon sugar.
Mix together and put on heat

00:27:40.895 --> 00:27:45.868
100 g chopped onion
(I substituted leeks)

00:27:46.917 --> 00:27:55.048
1/2 cup soup stock, 300g potatoes

00:28:08.838 --> 00:28:15.743
Make miso soup with the rest of dashi broth.

00:28:22.496 --> 00:28:33.815
A cup of white miso for dressing and a spoonful for miso soup.

00:28:36.128 --> 00:28:42.266
I also add some leftover avocado from the morning.

00:28:49.362 --> 00:29:00.375
When the potatoes are cooked, mash them.

00:29:04.336 --> 00:29:09.800
Mix mayonnaise with white soybean paste.

00:29:13.451 --> 00:29:25.689
When the potatoes are heated through, stuff them into fried tofu.

00:29:27.656 --> 00:29:37.963
I made a lot of it and ate it for three days.
If I reheat it on the fish grill, the fried bean curd gets crispy and it's good all the way through.

00:29:50.637 --> 00:29:57.572
Add salt and boil quickly.

00:30:42.742 --> 00:30:51.087
Kitsune croquettes with deep-fried tofu instead of batter.

00:30:53.466 --> 00:31:00.830
I liked how easy and crispy they were to fry and how easy they were to wash.

00:31:28.708 --> 00:31:37.360
White miso, mayonnaise, cheese
This recipe went well with bitter spring vegetables!

00:31:47.543 --> 00:31:55.735
burdock root are good smell.

00:32:14.234 --> 00:32:21.077
It was a menu that filled me up.

00:32:42.080 --> 00:32:55.514
I finished breakfast with yesterday's leftovers.
I'm rearranging the drawers that have been bothering me for a long time.

00:33:01.674 --> 00:33:14.035
I was thinking of moving it to a larger storage area because it's overflowing with cutlery.

00:33:19.299 --> 00:33:33.990
I decided to try a diagonal storage case because it looked like a good idea.

00:33:50.697 --> 00:33:58.275
perfect fit.
Every time I open the drawer my heart is soothed 🥰 lol

00:34:01.592 --> 00:34:12.175
I'd better leave the wooden spoons outside.
I decided to put it in the empty jar for now.

00:34:13.679 --> 00:34:20.277
I have to be careful not to lose the case that's provided.

00:35:15.862 --> 00:35:23.165
I can't go wrong with salted kelp in sweet zenzai.

00:35:25.310 --> 00:35:31.326
Thank you for watching to the end!

